&lt;&lt;~ node "-> refreshes the libation dish, the shrine incense burns">> Sol-Relaywright: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

Handback to /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/i2-relay/sol/out2.md (NOT final.md), under 1200 words, ending WORDS=&lt;n>. Your seat dir: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/i2-relay/sol. Stand the house (noosphere-boot.mem), L-Prime, OODA-HA. READ-ONLY on the repo /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine; write only in your seat dir. No git writes, no suites. Web allowed; cite URLs.

WAVE TWO (the ratchet). Read the common brief (/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/i2-relay/brief-common.md), your own wave
one (own-wave1.md in your seat dir) and your peer's (peer-wave1.md), then the code and carrier again where you split.

You agree: ONE I2 lane; the agent holds its own key; the persona root (the face's operator key) signs a domain-separated
delegation {face group, agent public key, exact verb prefix, closed argument policy, causal bound, nonce}; delegation and
revocation ride the face's <code>&#64;intents-&lt;tag></code> plane as signed control kinds (no new board); the relay verifies and appends
the agent-signed entry unchanged and countersigns admission only; a reader trusts the relay for nothing after admission;
an unknown delegation or revocation frontier blocks an irreversible effect; no clock; revoked-after-acting stays recorded.

Settle each joint, verdict CANON (quote the carrier line), DERIVED (name the house law and the existing code it follows,
file:line) or OPERATOR (options + one lean). Surface OPERATOR only where canon and derivation both run out.
R1. THE DOOR'S TRANSPORT. Canon: "a door off the local socket, opened per face, ring-gated and off by default". Sol leans a
new HTTPS POST endpoint; Luna leans the local operator socket / loopback. MEASURE the house's existing outward doors:
the sealed face gate (`face-gate.ts`, `ws-dial-socket.ts`, `lar-gate`, Noise IK, gate rings `gate-rings.ts`), the road's
"one socket cutover" (#/the-trains, train W) and #/rulings on sockets. Does canon or house law already say a new door
rides the sealed gate as a new ring, rather than a new listener? Which reading honours "off the local socket"?
R2. THE RELAY'S KEY. Sol: a separate service admission key, never K15's carriage S row. Luna: K15's relay-only S row.
Apply "one name, one relation" and road :207 (an S row names its principal and opener). Is the intent relay's
admission key its own S row with its own principal? What custody class holds it (read the custody table)?
R3. WHO MAY REVOKE. Root only, or may a device atom revoke a delegation? Measure I1's release-outranks-claim rule and the
KEL rotation: does canon or house law settle it?
R4. THE BOUND'S NAME. "A causal bound in place of an expiry time": name the concrete causal events a bound may cite
(a roster act CID, a K17 frontier head, a count of admitted invocations?) and how a reader that lacks the cited event
reads (waits, as I1's `every` does).
R5. ORDER AND OVERLAP. K15 bonds runs NOW (every face operation signs by the selected atom; a relay-only S row for
carriage; the opener's seed and identity hunks). D2 is landing (port lease, page transport). The hands room's lanes
follow K15 bonds. Can I2 run NOW beside K15 bonds, holding only intent-entry/read, the delegation verifier, the door
and its ring, and the relay service, taking no K15-held hunk? Name the exact files and the one opener hunk it needs.
Then restate the lane's slices, red-first, each red with its control and known positive.

